   176	## 3. The Poisson structure is globally symplectic
   177	
   178	The three brackets in (0.1) annihilate `q`, hence descend to `R`.  They have
   179	rank two everywhere: `{A,U}=2A^2` is nonzero on `D(A)`, while on `A=0`
   180	the equation gives `U=0` and `{U,Z}=2`.
   181	
   182	Let `omega` be the inverse symplectic form.  On `D(A)` it is
   183	
   184	```text
   185	omega=dA wedge dU/(2A^2).                              (3.1)
   186	```
   187	
   188	The alternative expressions using `(A,Z)` or `(U,Z)` show that (3.1)
   189	extends regularly and nowhere vanishing across `P`.  In particular every
   190	Hamiltonian vector field preserves it:
   191	
   192	```text
   193	L_(X_H) omega=d(i_(X_H)omega)=d(+/- dH)=0.             (3.2)
   194	```
   195	
   196	This is the essential extra hypothesis missing from a generic derivation
   197	with a slice.
