    85	finite cyclic cover before deleting `mu-1` lines.  The retained open is `A2`
    86	and maps surjectively and etale to `U` with generic degree `mu`.
    87	
    88	The retained map is not finite and need not be stable under the full deck
    89	action; the Galois assertion belongs to the finite cover and function-field
    90	level.  The induced `A1`-fibration on the retained `A2` is smooth with every
    91	scheme fibre an affine line.  The standard smooth-`A1`-bundle theorem over a
    92	regular curve, followed by `Pic(A1)=H^1(A1,O)=0`, trivializes it and makes its
    93	base parameter a polynomial coordinate `x`.  Hence
    94	
    95	```text
    96	rho o f_mu=a+lambda*x^mu.                               (2.1)
    97	```
    98	
    99	Both `f_mu` and `pi|U` are etale on their displayed domains, though neither
   100	is finite there.  Their composite is a polynomial local isomorphism; its
   101	nowhere-zero polynomial Jacobian is constant.  Surjectivity of `f_mu`, the
   102	quartic field tower, and the exact companion image give
   103	
   104	```text
   105	deg_geo(H)=4mu,             H(A2)=A2-{n}.               (2.2)
   106	```
   107	
   108	For an original counterexample chosen with minimal geometric degree,
   109	minimality gives `4mu>=4d1`, while the pseudo-plane Kummer step gives
   110	`mu|d1`; therefore `mu=d1`.  In the exact canonical `d1=1` specialization
   111	of this row, `mu|1` contradicts `mu>=2`.  No arbitrary rank-four `d1=1`
   112	statement outside this package follows.
   113	
   114	## 3. Boundary budget and the second asymptotic curve
   115	
   116	Normalize `Y` in the finite cyclic cover.  The retained `A2` has boundary
   117	equal to the inverse image of `R=Y-U` plus the deleted lines.  The first part
   118	maps to `B`; all deleted lines map to `C0=pi(Phi)`.  Thus
   119	
   120	```text
   121	NonProper(H)=B union C0.                                (3.1)
   122	```
   123	
   124	There is no hidden boundary divisor.  Also `n notin C0`, because the retained
   125	line is in the source while `H(A2)=A2-{n}`.
   126	
   127	Orevkov's formula must be applied on a regular extension.  Resolution only
   128	refines the finite-normalization boundary packets and cannot lower their
   129	contributions.  If `r=#Irr(B)`, generic ramified rank costs `2mu*r`; the
   130	unibranch `(3,1)` cusp costs another `mu`; and the `mu-1` deleted lines cost at
   131	least `mu-1`.  The two-preimage `(2,2)` node is budget-free because it changes
   132	the image identification, not the local degree along either normalization
   133	branch.  Consequently
   134	
   135	```text
   136	4mu-1 >= 2mu*r+mu+(mu-1)=2mu*r+2mu-1.                  (3.2)
   137	```
   138	
   139	Therefore `r=1` and equality holds in every contribution.  Now `C0!=B`.
   140	Equality makes every deleted line degree one over the `A1` normalization of
   141	`C0`, without finite ramification; etaleness makes that normalization map
   142	immersive.  Chau Theorem 4.4 forces singularity of the asymptotic image
   143	curve, not criticality of its parametrization.  Hence the singularity is a
   144	multibranch self-identification, giving the collision stated in Section 0.
   145	
   146	## 4. Exact Euler/orbit ledger and firewalls
   147	
   148	The full cyclic pullback of `T` has Euler number `mu*e(T)=-3mu`.  Removing
   149	the `mu-1` copies of the finite set `A` proves the first two identities in
   150	(0.1).  The map `x:D->A1` is quasi-finite: a vertical component would map
   151	onto the irreducible `B` and therefore contain its omitted point `n`.  A
   152	finite flat completion shows every special fibre has at most its generic
   153	cardinality.  Nonzero exceptional values occur in free cyclic orbits;
   154	constructible Euler integration then gives the last identity in (0.1).
   155	
   156	The valid residue statement is `e(D)=N mod mu`; neither `mu|e(D)`, `mu|3`,
   157	nor `N=0` follows.  The producer's all-`mu` hyperelliptic family realizes the
   158	Euler/orbit ledger with one cusp orbit and no bad ambient ruling fibre.  It is
   159	only a polynomial-fibre firewall: it does not realize a Keller pair, quartic
   160	algebra, omitted node, companion census, pseudo-plane Picard group, or
   161	canonical package.
   162	
   163	## 5. Exact remaining gate
   164	
   165	The cheapest live successor is the saturated two-component link at infinity
   166	of `B union C0`, charged together with the quartic companion algebra.  A
   167	successful theorem must do at least one of:
   168	
   169	1. force the `C0` self-identification onto `B` and derive an incompatible
   170	   divisor/intersection packet;
   171	2. force a critical boundary jump, contradicting saturation of (3.2);
   172	3. force a second reducible ruling fibre, contradicting `Q=0`; or
   173	4. compute `N` incompatibly with (0.1).
   174	
